ae="Kahana and Bibring described seven types: orderly-controlled, dependent-overdemanding, dramatizing-emotional, long-suffering self-sacrificing, guarded-querulous, superior-feeling, and uninvolved-aloof. For guarded-querulous patients, illness threatens their sense of safety. Transparent communication and respect for their need for control work better than reassurance or confrontation.",
